      "description": "Watch Santa Clara vs Nacional highlights and goals from Primeira Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 10, 2026. The atmosphere was electric on August 10, 2026, as Santa Clara hosted Nacional in a highly anticipated Primeira Liga encounter. Both teams entered the pitch with clear tactical intentions, setting the stage for a compelling battle of wits and skill. Early Dominance for Santa Clara The match ignited early as Santa Clara looked to capitalize on their home-field advantage. In the 17th minute, Daniel Borges nearly produced a contender for goal of the season with a spectacular bicycle kick, only to be denied by a brilliant save from Renato Marin . However, the pressure finally told in the 19th minute. Capitalizing on a defensive lapse by Joel da Silva , Gonçalo Paciência clinical finished to give the hosts the lead. Just two minutes later, Paciência was at it again, doubling the advantage with a powerful header following a pinpoint corner from Diogo Calila . Nacional’s Resilient Response Just as Santa Clara seemed to be cruising, the momentum shifted dramatically in favor of Nacional . In the 35th minute, Guilherme Romão conceded a penalty for a trip on Markus Gustav Jensen . Liziero stepped up and coolly converted the spot-kick with his left foot to bring the visitors back into the game. The drama intensified just before the halftime whistle when Miguel Baeza found space to fire home an equalizer. A tense VAR review followed, but the goal was ultimately confirmed, leaving the scores level at the break after a breathless opening 45 minutes. A Tactical Second Half The second half proved to be a tighter affair as both managers adjusted their setups. The game became increasingly physical, leading to a yellow card for Filipe Soares in the 70th minute for unsportsmanlike conduct. A flurry of tactical substitutions followed, with Santa Clara introducing Lucas Soares and Nacional bringing on Tiago Ribeiro to find a late winner. Despite the fresh legs, clear-cut chances were hard to come by. Santa Clara pushed for a winner in stoppage time, but a blocked shot from Lucas Soares ensured that both sides walked away with a hard-earned point in a game of two halves."
